    post {
        success {
            githubNotify status: 'SUCCESS', description: 'All checks passed'
        }
        failure {
            githubNotify status: 'FAILURE', description: 'CI pipeline failed'
        }
        always {
            cleanWs()
        }
    }
}
```

This uses the `githubNotify` step which is part of the GitHub plugin. When Jenkins runs on a PR (via `changeRequest()`), it will report the status back to GitHub. The GitHub repo needs branch protection rules to require this status check before merging.

